        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(ui): surface self-learning toggle in the Skill Workshop tab",
        "body": "Closes #106054\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\n`skills.workshop.autonomous.enabled` (self-learning: autonomous Skill Workshop capture, extended by #105674 to post-run experience review) is config/CLI-only. It is off by default because it spends extra background tokens, so the users who would benefit never find it: a settings key with no UI surface is invisible.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe setting's payoff is the Workshop proposal board, so the toggle lives there instead of a global settings page:\n\n- **Header toggle** \"Self-learning\" in the Workshop tab header, next to the existing view controls. It reflects the current config value and doubles as a status answer to \"why did no proposal appear?\". It hides until the config snapshot is loaded so it never flashes a wrong state.\n- **Empty-state pitch card** on the empty proposal board: a short explanation naming the token-cost tradeoff and that drafts arrive as pending proposals, plus an Enable button. This reaches curious users at the moment they are already looking for proposals.\n\nBoth surfaces write the canonical config key through the existing `runtimeConfig.patch` seam (RFC 7396 merge patch against the current snapshot hash), then refresh the snapshot. Patch failures surface in the workshop error banner and the checkbox reverts to the config value. No new config surface, no duplicate settings-page toggle.\n\nTo respect the TypeScript LOC ratchet, the oversized workshop files were split along cohesive seams: `empty-states.ts`, `header-controls.ts`, and `self-learning.ts` (view.ts 1137 -> 1005, skill-workshop-page.ts 700 -> 661; baseline moved down accordingly).\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can discover and enable self-learning from the Workshop tab in the Control UI instead of hand-editing `openclaw.json` or knowing the CLI incantation. The setting remains off by default; the pitch copy states the extra token cost and that drafts arrive as pending proposals (deliberately no unconditional review guarantee, which would be false under skills.workshop.approvalPolicy \"auto\").\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox (fresh lease, synced head): `pnpm test ui/src/pages/skill-workshop` green, then full ui suite via check lanes: 234 test files / 3734 tests passed, including three new tests: header toggle reflects config / hides without a snapshot, empty-state enable issues the exact merge patch and refreshes, patch failure surfaces the error banner and keeps the toggle off.\n- Blacksmith Testbox `check:changed`: conflict markers, TypeScript LOC ratchet, changelog attributions, wildcard re-export guards, duplicate coverage, dependency pins, oxfmt format lanes all ok on the final head; hosted PR CI re-runs the full lane fan-out.\n- Fresh autoreview (Codex gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh): clean, no accepted/actionable findings (\"patch is correct, 0.85\").\n- Docs: `docs/tools/skill-workshop.md` notes the Control UI toggle next to the existing enablement paragraph.\n\n- Second autoreview round (slim branch, Codex gpt-5.6-sol xhigh): copy overclaim under approvalPolicy \"auto\" accepted and fixed; $include display concern rejected with source proof (snapshot sourceConfig/resolved are both include-resolved, src/config/io.ts).\n",
